# Pose-control checks on the booted device (evidence: devicectl-cli.log):
# - `simctl io <UDID> enumerate` lists two integrated screens: (1) "LCD",
#   1398x2034 px, device name "primary" (the outer display), and (3) "LCD-1",
#   2007x2853 px, "primary-1" (the inner display).
# - `simctl io <UDID> screenConfig --display=1 power off` printed
#   "Screen 1 power state set to off". The inner display stayed black, so this
#   is not a fold. After `power on`, the outer display stayed black until the
#   device was shut down and booted again. Do not use it.
# - `xcrun devicectl device info displays` reports per-display `active` and
#   `backlightState`. Closed pose: LCD active, LCD-1 "backlight is off".
